IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rra-nouns`
IMPORT `rra-logic`
IMPORT `rra-part1-preliminary`

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 July 2022 -- PART 2 PRESCRIBED MINIMUM RETIREMENT AGE (ss 4 to 6).

§ `Part 2 -- Prescribed minimum retirement age`

§§ `Section 4(2) -- no dismissal on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age`

-- src:281 | (2) Despite any other written law, contract of service or collective
-- src:282 | agreement, an employer must not dismiss an employee on the ground
-- src:283 | of age before that employee attains the employee’s prescribed
-- src:284 | minimum retirement age.
@ref s 4(2) (src:281-284)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the dismissal is on the ground of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the dismissal` IS A DATE
      `a written law, contract of service or collective agreement says otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(2) the employer may dismiss the employee on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age` MEANS
    -- "Despite any other written law, contract of service or collective agreement": no limb reads
    -- `a written law, contract of service or collective agreement says otherwise`, which is what "despite" says.
    CONSIDER `s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` (employment's `date of birth`) (employment's `prescribed minimum retirement age`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the date on which the employee attains the prescribed minimum retirement age cannot be worked out (29 February birth, no anniversary date)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST attained THEN
        IF `the dismissal is on the ground of age` AND `the date of the dismissal` LESS THAN attained
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an employer must not dismiss an employee on the ground of age before that employee attains the employee's prescribed minimum retirement age"
            JUST FALSE
        ELSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is of a dismissal "on the ground of age" and "before" the employee attains the prescribed minimum retirement age; the case falls outside both limits
            NOTHING

-- src:281 | (2) Despite any other written law, contract of service or collective
-- src:282 | agreement, an employer must not dismiss an employee on the ground
-- src:283 | of age before that employee attains the employee’s prescribed
-- src:284 | minimum retirement age.
@ref s 4(2) (src:281-284)
GIVEN `the day the employee attains the prescribed minimum retirement age` IS A DATE
      `the day the clock starts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`s 4(2) the employer shall not dismiss the employee on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age` MEANS
    -- The clock counts days from `the day the clock starts`.  The prohibition holds up to and including the day
    -- before the employee attains the age ("before that employee attains"), so it lapses at that day minus one.
    IF `the day the employee attains the prescribed minimum retirement age` AT MOST `the day the clock starts`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY Employer
         SHANT `dismiss the employee on the ground of age`
         WITHIN (Day `the day the employee attains the prescribed minimum retirement age` MINUS Day `the day the clock starts` MINUS 1)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Employer BECAUSE "s 4(2): the employee was dismissed on the ground of age before attaining the prescribed minimum retirement age"

§§ `Section 4(1) -- the Minister specifies the prescribed minimum retirement age`

-- The age itself is specified by the Minister by notification in the Gazette and is not among the sources, so it is a
-- fact the case supplies (Employment, `prescribed minimum retirement age`); the Act's own limits on what may be specified
-- are 62 and 65.
-- src:274 | 4.—(1) The Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, specify
-- src:275 | the prescribed minimum retirement age applicable to any class of
-- src:276 | employees, which must be at least 62 years but not more than 65
-- src:277 | years.
@ref s 4(1) (src:274-277)
GIVEN `the age specified` IS A NUMBER
      `the age is specified by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) the age specified may be the prescribed minimum retirement age` MEANS
    IF `the age specified` LESS THAN 62 OR `the age specified` GREATER THAN 65
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which must be at least 62 years but not more than 65 years" -- a requirement read as closing the range (marginal reading (a))
        JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the age is specified by notification in the Gazette`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Minister "may, by notification in the Gazette, specify"; the age is within the range but was not specified in that way
            NOTHING

§§ `Section 4(3) -- the offence of dismissing before the prescribed minimum retirement age`

-- src:288 | (3) An employer who contravenes subsection (2) shall be guilty of
-- src:289 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:290 | $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to
-- src:291 | both.
@ref s 4(3) (src:288-291)
GIVEN `the employer contravened subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(3) the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the employer contravened subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An employer who contravenes subsection (2) shall be guilty of an offence"; the employer did not contravene subsection (2)
        NOTHING

@ref s 4(3) (src:288-291)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 4(3) the penalty on conviction` MEANS Penalty OF 5_000, 6

@ref s 4(3) (src:288-291)
GIVEN `the employer has been convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(3) the sentence is within the penalty` MEANS
    IF NOT `the employer has been convicted`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is one the employer is "liable on conviction" to; there has been no conviction
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the fine and the term are within the ceilings` (`s 4(3) the penalty on conviction`) `the fine in dollars` `the imprisonment in months`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both"
            JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 6 -- invalidity of a term of a contract of service or collective agreement`

-- "made before, on or after 1 July 1993": the date on which the term was made is not a limb of the rule.
-- src:299 | 6. Any term of a contract of service or collective agreement made
-- src:300 | before, on or after 1 July 1993 which provides for a retirement age
-- src:301 | which is below the employee’s prescribed minimum retirement age is
-- src:302 | void to the extent that it is so less favourable.
@ref s 6 (src:299-302)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the term is in a contract of service or a collective agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the retirement age the term provides for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 the term is void` MEANS
    IF `the term is in a contract of service or a collective agreement` AND `the retirement age the term provides for` LESS THAN employment's `prescribed minimum retirement age`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 6 voids "any term of a contract of service or collective agreement ... which provides for a retirement age which is below the employee's prescribed minimum retirement age"; the term is not of that kind
        NOTHING

-- "void to the extent that it is so less favourable": the term stands as far as it reaches the prescribed minimum
-- retirement age and no further, so the retirement age it leaves standing is the higher of the two.
@ref s 6 (src:299-302)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the retirement age the term provides for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 6 the retirement age that the term leaves standing` MEANS
    max `the retirement age the term provides for` (employment's `prescribed minimum retirement age`)
